It's the "Breibart index", a way of measuring spamminess; you can google for
it if you like.

Let's analyze your posts with it.

The index is defined as the sum of the square roots of the number of
newsgroups a given identical message has been posted to; if you crosspost
it twice, first to 4 groups and then to 16, the index will be
sqrt(4)+sqrt(16)=6.
If you post it separately to all 20 groups, though, the index will be
sqrt(1)+sqrt(1).... 20 times, and thus 20.

(The definition of "identical" varies; mine is fairly liberal, ignoring
quotes and signatures.)

A message is defined as severe spam, and thus eligible for
auto-cancellation, if the index is 20 or greater. Also, my slightly hacked
newsreader checks it automatically and puts a 1 month killfile on anyone
who crosses it.

In your case, it's collected 5 identical "message ignored" notes, none of
which were crossposted; this amounts to an index of 5*sqrt(1).

You still have some way to go before crossing the boundary.


